6,Research Guides: Modern Tibetan Studies Research Guide: Music,https://guides.library.columbia.edu/c.php?g=1434781&p=10652846,"The resource provides a wealth of materials for the interdisciplinary study of ethnomusicology; whether the focus is on music, anthropology, dance, religion or spirituality. Recordings of Tibetan music are primarily in two collections: Fredric Lieberman Collection (Sikkim, 1970); and the Peter Crossley-Holland Collection (Sikkim and Ladakh,1961).",Koyee,Sino-Tibetan
7,Tibetan Music Preservation | Traditional and Classical Music,https://tibetanmusicpreservation.wordpress.com/,"Tibetan Music Preservation (TMP) is an online initiative to preserve and promote endangered Tibetan traditional music. TMP projects include audio and video recordings of traditional and classical music, interviews of traditional artists. These online archives are free of charge for the public to access.",Koyee,Sino-Tibetan
8,Koi language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/koi_language,"Koyee (कोयी), also known as Koi or Koyu, is an endangered Sino-Tibetan language of the Kiranti branch spoken by the Koyu Rai people in the Khotang District of eastern Nepal. [1] With 4,152 native speakers according to the 2021 Nepal census, it is classified as vulnerable [2] and primarily used in rural hill communities like Sungdel village, where it serves ritual, familial, and daily ...",Koyee,Sino-Tibetan
9,Getting to Know: Tenzin Choegyal - Street Talk,https://thestreetcbr.wordpress.com/2024/03/26/getting-to-know-tenzin-choegyal/,"GETTING TO KNOW: TENZIN CHOEGYAL Singer-songwriter, activist and cultural ambassador Tenzin Choegyal is considered one of the world's finest musicians in the Tibetan tradition. A son of Tibetan nomads, Tenzin feels a particular connection to the music of the wandering people of the Tibetan plateau.",Koyee,Sino-Tibetan
